# Spec — Phase 4: Campaign Export (schema + section registry)

Repo: `veydria-cartography`. You are implementing in an isolated git worktree; 
nothing
reaches the real tree until reviewed. **Touch only the files named in this spec
.**
The persistence foundation already exists and must not be redesigned.

## Goal

The app stores GM campaign state across ~12 browser keys via a synchronous faca
de
(`kvStore`). Today it is **export-only, no import**. Phase 4 builds the **read 
side**:
a single serializable campaign envelope + a section registry so adding a future
feature = one registry entry. **No GUI, no file I/O, no Blob/download** — pure 
logic,
fully unit-testable. (Import orchestration and UI are Phase 5; do not build the
m.)

## Background you must respect (already built — do NOT change)

`web/src/persistence/`:
- `kv-store.ts` — `kvStore` singleton, synchronous: `getString(key): string|nul
l`,
  `setString(key, value): void`, `remove(key): void`, `keys(): string[]`. All s
tores
  route through it. Default backend is localStorage (zero-setup), so tests need
no hydrate.
- `provider.ts` — `VEYDRIA_KEY_PREFIX = 'veydria'`, `isVeydriaKey(key)`.

Every store keeps its **exact current signatures, keys, and embedded migrations
**.
You will REUSE the existing `load*`/`save*` functions (so their validators/migr
ations
run for free). The only new exports you add to existing util files are two coll
ection
setters (`setStarredIds`, `setPrepDoneIds`); plus you create a small new `hex-s
ize.ts`
helper module. Do not centralize or alter any existing migration.

## Verified store inventory — the registry source of truth

**`content` scope (portable / shareable across machines):**

| id | storageKey | existing read | existing write (collection setter) |
|---|---|---|---|
| annotations | `veydria-annotations-v2` | `loadAnnotations(): MapAnnotation[]`
| `saveAnnotations(a): void` |
| journeys | `veydria.journeys.v1` | `loadSavedJourneys(): SavedJourney[]` | `s
aveJourneys(e): void` |
| featureNotes | `veydria.featureNotes.v1` | `loadFeatureNotes(): FeatureNotes`
| `saveFeatureNotes(m): void` |
| stars | `veydria.stars.v1` | `getStarredIds(): string[]` | ⚠️ **ADD `setStarre
dIds(ids: string[]): void`** |
| prepOrder | `veydria.prepOrder.v1` | `getPrepOrder(): string[]` | `setPrepOrd
er(ids): void` |
| prepDone | `veydria.prepDone.v1` | `getPrepDoneIds(): string[]` | ⚠️ **ADD `se
tPrepDoneIds(ids: string[]): void`** |
| featureHooks | `veydria.hooks.v1` | `loadFeatureHooks(): Record<string, Featu
reHook[]>` | `saveFeatureHooks(m): void` |
| layerPresets | `veydria.layer.presets.v1` | `loadCustomPresets(): LayerPreset
[]` | `saveCustomPresets(p): void` |

Files: `web/src/utils/{annotations,journey-saved,feature-notes,feature-stars,se
ssion-prep,feature-hooks,layer-presets}.ts`.

**`preference` scope (machine-local, full-backup only — never shared):**

| id | storageKey | read | write |
|---|---|---|---|
| timeOfDay | `veydria.timeOfDay.v1` | `loadTimeOfDay(): TimeOfDay` | `saveTime
OfDay(v): void` (raw enum string) |
| hexSize | `veydria.hexSize` | (inline in App.tsx — see below) | (inline — raw
number string) |
| aiLoreSettings | `veydria.aiLoreSettings.v1` | `loadAiLoreSettings(): AiLoreS
ettings` | `saveAiLoreSettings(s): void` |

> **apiKey sanitization is owned by the export READ side, not the writer.** `sa
veAiLoreSettings`
> must keep storing the real local key untouched. The `aiLoreSettings` registry
`read()` returns
> the settings object **with the `apiKey` property absent** (see §2). Do NOT ch
ange `saveAiLoreSettings`.

Files: `web/src/utils/{time-of-day,ai-lore}.ts`, `web/src/App.tsx`.

**Excluded entirely — these keys must NEVER appear in an export:**
`veydria.aiLoreCache.v1`, `veydria.search.recent.v1`, `veydria.tour.completed.v
1`,
`veydria.journey.tutorial.completed.v1`, `veydria.sessionActive.v1`.

## Files to CREATE (all in `web/src/persistence/`)

### 1. `campaign-schema.ts`
- `export const CURRENT_CAMPAIGN_VERSION = 1`
- Envelope type:
  ```ts
  export interface CampaignEnvelope {
    schema: 'veydria-campaign'
    version: number
    savedAt: number
    content: Record<string, unknown>        // keyed by content section id; omi
ts empty sections
    preferences?: Record<string, unknown>   // keyed by preference section id; 
omitted if empty
  }
  ```
- `export function migrateCampaign(json: unknown): CampaignEnvelope` — the impo
rt-side gate.
  Throw (human-readable message — surfaces in a P5 toast) unless ALL hold:
  - `json` is a non-null object;
  - `json.schema === 'veydria-campaign'`;
  - `json.version === 1` (the ONLY known version — this single check rejects `>
1`, `< 1`,
    `0`, non-integer, missing, and non-number in one stroke);
  - `typeof json.savedAt === 'number'`;
  - `json.content` is a non-null object.
  On success return `json` typed as `CampaignEnvelope`. Phase 4 only defines + 
unit-tests
  this; it is not yet wired to any importer.

### 2. `section-registry.ts` — implement EXACTLY this interface (do not redesig
n)
```ts
export type SectionScope = 'content' | 'preference'
export type ImportMode = 'replace' | 'merge'   // ImportMode is DEFINED here, n
ot imported

export interface CampaignSection<T = unknown> {
  id: string
  storageKey: string
  scope: SectionScope
  read(): T | undefined          // see the single empty-rule below
  write(value: T, mode: ImportMode): void
}

export const CAMPAIGN_SECTIONS: CampaignSection[]
```
Rules:
- One entry per inventory row, reusing the existing `load*`/`save*`/setter func
tions.
- **The single empty rule (applies to EVERY section, no per-section sentinels):
**
  `read()` returns `undefined` **iff `kvStore.getString(storageKey) === null`**
(the key was
  never written). Otherwise it returns the value from the store's `load*()`/get
ter (so the
  embedded validator still runs). This is robust and unambiguous — do not inven
t per-store
  "is this the default value" checks. (A store that legitimately persisted `[]`
will be
  omitted too; that's the intended "no empty noise" behavior.)
- aiLoreSettings `read()`: when the key exists, return `loadAiLoreSettings()` w
ith the
  **`apiKey` property absent** — use object rest to omit it: `const { apiKey, .
..rest } = s; return rest`.
  The property must be ABSENT (not `null`/`undefined`-valued). This is the sing
le
  security-critical line.
- hexSize: **extract a shared helper** to avoid duplicating the `[30,50,70]`/de
fault-`50`
  whitelist. Create `web/src/utils/hex-size.ts` exporting `loadHexSize(): numbe
r` and
  `saveHexSize(n: number): void`, mirroring the current App.tsx logic EXACTLY:
  `loadHexSize` = read `kvStore.getString('veydria.hexSize')`; if null/falsy re
turn `50`;
  `const n = Number.parseInt(stored, 10)` (radix 10); return `[30,50,70].includ
es(n) ? n : 50`.
  `saveHexSize(n)` = `kvStore.setString('veydria.hexSize', String(n))`. No othe
r behavior.
  Then update App.tsx to call these (below). The hexSize section follows the si
ngle empty
  rule (undefined iff the key is absent), so it reads `loadHexSize()` when pres
ent.
- `write(value, mode)`: for `mode === 'replace'`, call the store's collection s
etter
  (`saveAnnotations`, `setStarredIds`, etc.). For `mode === 'merge'`,
  `throw new Error('merge not implemented (Phase 5)')`. **Export never calls `w
rite`**, so
  in Phase 4 the `write` paths are NOT separately tested beyond the two new set
ters' own
  unit tests (§ tests 5–6) — the other sections delegate to already-tested `sav
e*` functions,
  and full import is Phase 5. `write` only needs to compile and type-check here
.

### 3. `campaign-export.ts`
```ts
export function exportCampaign(): CampaignEnvelope
```
- Iterate `CAMPAIGN_SECTIONS`; call `read()` on each; collect non-`undefined` r
esults into
  `content` (scope `'content'`) or `preferences` (scope `'preference'`), keyed 
by `section.id`.
- Set `schema: 'veydria-campaign'`, `version: CURRENT_CAMPAIGN_VERSION`, `saved
At: Date.now()`.
- Omit the `preferences` field entirely if no preference sections produced a va
lue.
- Pure assembly. No JSON.stringify, no Blob, no download. Return the object.

## Files to MODIFY (surgical — add only; signatures/keys/migrations unchanged)

### `web/src/utils/feature-stars.ts`
Add, reusing the existing private `readStars`/`writeStars` and `MAX_STARS` (= 5
0):
```ts
export function setStarredIds(ids: string[]): void
```
Must preserve store invariants: filter to strings only, dedupe keeping **first
occurrence** (most-recent-first order), cap at `MAX_STARS` (50), then `writeSta
rs(...)`.
Do NOT blind-write the raw array. (This is the most likely place to get it wron
g.)

### `web/src/utils/session-prep.ts`
Add, reusing the existing private `writeDone`:
```ts
export function setPrepDoneIds(ids: string[]): void
```
Filter to strings only, dedupe keeping first occurrence (preserve order), then 
`writeDone(...)`.
(No cap; done-state is unbounded by design.)

### `web/src/App.tsx` (~lines 373–380)
Replace the inline hexSize read/write with the new `loadHexSize()` / `saveHexSi
ze()`
from `web/src/utils/hex-size.ts`. Behavior must be identical. Do not touch anyt
hing else.

## Tests to ADD (this is the acceptance gate — must be green)

Use vitest. Match the existing localStorage-stub convention from
`web/src/utils/feature-stars.test.ts` (install an in-memory `localStorage` stub
at module
load; `localStorage.clear()` in `beforeEach`). Seed stores by calling their `sa
ve*` functions
(preferred — exercises real validators) or `localStorage.setItem(KEY, json)`.

`web/src/persistence/campaign-export.test.ts`:
1. **Round-trip completeness** — seed all 8 content stores (via their `save*`/s
etter fns)
   and the 3 preferences (seed aiLoreSettings via `saveAiLoreSettings` with a p
opulated
   object; set hexSize via `saveHexSize(70)`; set timeOfDay via `saveTimeOfDay(
'night')`);
   `exportCampaign()`; assert every expected section id is present under the co
rrect
   top-level key (`content.annotations`, …, `preferences.hexSize`, …) with the 
seeded values.
2. **Envelope constants** — on a populated export assert `schema === 'veydria-c
ampaign'`,
   `version === 1`, `typeof savedAt === 'number'`, and `content` is always an o
bject (present).
3. **🔒 apiKey absent** — `saveAiLoreSettings({ apiKey: 'sk-SECRET-123', endpoi
nt:'…', model:'…', temperature: 0.7 })`;
   assert `JSON.stringify(exportCampaign())` does **not** contain `'sk-SECRET-1
23'` AND
   `exportCampaign().preferences.aiLoreSettings` has no own `apiKey` property
   (`'apiKey' in section === false`).
4. **Excluded keys absent** — seed the 5 excluded keys by raw `localStorage.set
Item` with the
   literal key strings (`'veydria.aiLoreCache.v1'`, `'veydria.search.recent.v1'
`,
   `'veydria.tour.completed.v1'`, `'veydria.journey.tutorial.completed.v1'`,
   `'veydria.sessionActive.v1'`) and unique sentinel values; assert none of tho
se sentinel
   values appear anywhere in `JSON.stringify(exportCampaign())`.
5. **Empty stores omitted** — with cleared storage, `exportCampaign().content` 
deep-equals `{}`
   and the envelope has **no `preferences` key** (`'preferences' in env === fal
se`).
6. **Stars setter invariants** — `setStarredIds([...60 ids])` → `getStarredIds(
).length === 50`
   and order preserved (first 50); `setStarredIds(['a','a','b'])` → `['a','b']`
;
   round-trips through `getStarredIds()`.
7. **prepDone setter** — `setPrepDoneIds(['x','y','x'])` → `getPrepDoneIds()` e
quals `['x','y']`
   (deduped, order preserved).

`web/src/persistence/campaign-schema.test.ts` (or co-located):
8. `migrateCampaign` accepts a valid `{ schema:'veydria-campaign', version:1, s
avedAt:0, content:{} }`
   (returns it). Throws on EACH of: `version: 2`; `version: 0`; missing `versio
n`;
   non-numeric `version`; wrong/missing `schema`; missing/non-number `savedAt`;
   `content` not an object; non-object input (`null`, a string).

## Verification (run in the worktree before declaring done)

```
cd web && npm test          # all existing tests + the new ones green
cd web && npx tsc -b         # typecheck clean
```
Do not run `npm run build`/`build:tauri` (slow) — tsc + tests are the gate.

## Out of scope (do NOT implement)
- Any import/restore logic beyond the `replace` setter calls and `migrateCampai
gn` stub.
  > Phase-5 flag (do not handle now): since export omits `apiKey`, a future `re
place` import
  > of `aiLoreSettings` must PRESERVE the user's existing local `apiKey` rather
than clobber
  > it with the absent property. Phase 5's concern — noted so it isn't lost.
- The `merge` branch (Phase 5), any UI/menu/button, any Blob/file-dialog/downlo
ad code,
  any Tauri/`tauri-fs-provider`/`flush()` work (Phase 6).
- Touching any file not named above.
